# BriefIQ Conventions

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for the full project context. This file is the lightweight always-on layer.

## Code style
- Files under 200 lines. Split when they grow.
- Clear, descriptive names. `runQueryCycle` not `processIt`.
- Comments are plentiful and explain WHY (intent, constraints, trade-offs).
- Avoid pure narration comments (`// increment counter`). Good naming covers the WHAT.
- Never delete old comments unless they are obviously obsolete or wrong.
- No emojis in code. UI strings are fine.

## File naming
- Backend: kebab-case with dot suffix — `auth.module.ts`, `jwt-auth.guard.ts`, `current-user.decorator.ts`.
- iOS: PascalCase — `FeedView.swift`, `BriefingCard.swift`.

## Errors
- Don't jump to conclusions. Consider multiple possible causes before fixing.
- Explain the problem in plain English first.
- Make minimal changes — change as few lines as needed.

## Tests
- Write a test for every meaningful change.
- Run tests after each change.
- Backend tests: `npm test` from `briefiq-api/`. iOS tests: Xcode `Cmd+U`.

## Simplicity
- Pick the simpler approach unless there's a concrete reason not to.
- Modular over clever.
- Focus on core functionality before optimization.

## Product philosophy (never violate)
- Silence is a feature. Empty briefings are valid output, not errors.
- Push only on real signal. Default to daily digest mode.
- Respect attention: honor quiet hours, Focus modes, interruption levels.
- Never repeat a briefing the user has already seen.
